  "never": [
    "dark mock-UI or app chrome in an illustrated video",
    "a frame of text with no picture",
    "a micrograph or schematic without its label (stain and magnification, or 'simplified picture')",
    "text under the layout's minimum size",
    "a number the viewer might act on drawn by hand: numbers are typeset",
    "a picture event smaller than about 70 x 70 px, or fading in slower than 6 frames, counted as the line's event",
    "a symbol with no words: a '?' or an unlabelled circle is the one mark a muted viewer cannot read",
    "a Latin or technical term without its meaning beside it (functio laesa \u00b7 loss of function)",
    "a number before the measure it belongs to is named (define SG before SG > 1.020)",
    "a stamp or label in a fixed corner, away from the thing it marks",
    "a channel ask in the middle of a chapter: asks go at a beat boundary or the end card"
  ]
